# Extensions (Gateways, Servers, Modules)

## Layout & namespace

```
extensions/Gateways/{Name}/Gateway.php  → Extensions\Gateways\{Name}\Gateway
extensions/Servers/{Name}/Server.php    → Extensions\Servers\{Name}\Server
extensions/Modules/{Name}/...           → Extensions\Modules\{Name}\...
```

Composer maps `Extensions\` → `extensions/`. Optional per-extension: views, lang, routes, migrations, config — loaded when the extension is **enabled** in the `extensions` table (`ExtensionServiceProvider`).

## Base classes (`app/Extensions/Foundation/`)

| Type | Extend | Must implement |
| --- | --- | --- |
| One-off payment gateway | `GatewayExtension` | `pay(Payment $payment, GatewayConfig $gatewayConfig)` |
| Recurring gateway | `SubscriptionGatewayExtension` | subscription pay/manage contract |
| Server panel | `ServerExtension` | `create/suspend/unsuspend/terminate(Order, ServerConnection)` + config hooks |
| Generic module | `ModuleExtension` | module-specific hooks |

Use Artisan makers under `app/Extensions/Commands/` (`MakeServerCommand`, `MakeModuleCommand`, etc.) when scaffolding.

## Eloquent vs runtime class

- `App\Models\Extension` (and scoped `Gateway` / `Server` / `Module`) store registry rows (`identifier`, `namespace`, `type`, `status`).
- Runtime configs: `GatewayConfig`, `ServerConnection` — not the extension class itself.
- Call through models: `$gateway->extension()->pay(...)`, `$order->serverMethods()->create(...)`.

## Webhooks & CSRF

- Gateway webhook/callback routes must stay under paths exempt from CSRF (`gateways/webhooks/*`, `gateways/callbacks/*` in `bootstrap/app.php`).
- Log/inspect with existing webhook log models where applicable; never trust webhook payloads without signature/verification patterns used by sibling gateways.

## Rules of thumb

- Mirror `extensions/Gateways/StripeCheckout` or `extensions/Servers/Pterodactyl` rather than inventing a new layout.
- Do not put panel/API HTTP clients in Actions — keep them inside the extension.
- After install/enable, ensure DB row + `config('app.installed')` so the provider loads the extension.
